I'll build this swimming practice as a Rhylthyme program. Let me analyze the structure:

**Key insights from the text:**
- All three lanes run in parallel for most activities
- Warm-up, whiteboard, kick, cooldown, debrief: all lanes together
- Main set: each lane independent (variable duration, 30–50 min)
- Sprint set: **serial** (one lane at a time, 10 min each) off shared starting blocks
- Sprints don't start until all lanes finish main set (implicit barrier)
- Total pool time budget: 150 minutes
- One coach on deck (can supervise, not a machine constraint)

**Program structure:**
- 3 parallel tracks (lanes 1, 2, 3)
- Shared steps (warm-up, whiteboard, kick, cooldown, debrief) use `programStart` or `afterStep` chained across tracks
- Main set per lane (variable)
- Sprint set: replicated step (count: 3, mode: serial) that waits for all lanes to finish main set first
- Constraints: 3 lanes, 1 set of blocks

